# Code owners for the Knowledge workspace.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# The crates listed here are the security-critical surfaces that
# need explicit review before a merge — the cryptography stack,
# the FFI surface that other languages link against, the
# persistent evidence store, and the security policy document.
#
# Order matters: later patterns override earlier ones. The catch-
# all at the very bottom is intentionally absent so we do not
# inadvertently expand the codeowner contract to crates the
# maintainers have not opted into.

# ---- Crypto crate ----
# Hybrid X25519 + ML-KEM-768 KEM, HKDF, XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD,
# zeroize discipline, ML-DSA-65 provenance signatures, SPHINCS+
# archival co-signing, and the new KeyStorage trait that sits in
# front of every hardware-backed key store the substrate uses.
# All changes require explicit review.
/crates/crypto/ @kennguy3n

# ---- FFI surface ----
# The UniFFI exports and the NAPI bindings together form the
# substrate's public contract against host platforms (Swift,
# Kotlin, TypeScript / Node). Breaking changes here propagate to
# every embedder; require explicit review.
/crates/ffi/  @kennguy3n
/crates/napi/ @kennguy3n

# ---- Evidence store ----
# SQLCipher-backed durable storage, FTS5 indexing, cryptographic
# forgetting via DEK destruction, ring buffer, schema migrations.
# Every change touches user data at rest; require explicit review.
/crates/evidence_store/ @kennguy3n

# ---- Security policy ----
# The threat model, audit scope, and vulnerability disclosure
# process. Required reviewer matches the crypto/ffi/storage
# triad so disclosure decisions stay coupled to the surfaces
# under review.
/SECURITY.md @kennguy3n
